course: dictionary
lesson: 1435
title: Words for people at work
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A carpenter is a person who makes and fixes wooden things. Read the sentence and look for clues: «Joseph was a carpenter who was told in a dream to take Mary as his wife and care for the child.» Carpenters build things from wood, so you can picture the job even if you have never met one.
explain: Some words describe the person and the skill. «A skilled carpenter» is someone who is good at the job because they have practised it. Carpenters measure, saw and build, so the words around carpenter tell you what they do.
explain: Some stories use the same word in different ways. Carpenter bees are not people at all. «Carpenter bees chew tunnels in wood for their nests.» The word carpenter is in the name because the bees work in wood, like a carpenter does. Read the words around the word to see whether the carpenter is a person or an animal.
fact: A carpenter is a person whose job is making and fixing wooden things.
fact: Carpenters make and fix things such as doors, floors, roofs, shelves and furniture.
fact: «A skilled carpenter» means a carpenter who is very good at the job.
fact: «John Harrison, a carpenter born in Yorkshire, built sea clocks in the 1700s.»
fact: Carpenter bees chew tunnels in wood and push the sawdust out instead of eating it.
exercise: «Joseph was a carpenter who was told in a dream to take Mary as his wife.» What is a carpenter? | *A person who makes and fixes wooden things | A person who sells paintings | A person who keeps bees in a garden | A person who sails ships across the sea
exercise: A carpenter has a plank of wood 8 metres long and cuts it into 4 equal pieces. How long is each piece? | *2 metres | 8 metres | 1 metre | 4 metres
exercise: In «a skilled carpenter», which word tells you the carpenter is good at the job? | carpenter | *skilled | a | the
test: «John Harrison, a carpenter born in Yorkshire, built sea clocks in the 1700s.» What was John Harrison's job? | Painter | Sailor | Farmer | *Carpenter
test: The sea clocks built by John Harrison helped sailors find what? | What the weather would be | How deep the sea was | *How far east or west they were | Where the best fish were
exam: «Qi Baishi was a carpenter before becoming a painter.» What did Qi Baishi do before he became a painter? | *He was a carpenter | He was a sailor | He was a teacher | He was a beekeeper
